      "Starter Motor Burnout: Caused by endlessly cranking the engine trying to overcome the hot start issue or air leaks in the fuel lines.",
      "Fuel System Air Leaks: Aging rubber fuel return lines allow air to enter the high-pressure system, causing rough running and stalling.",
      "Severe Drivetrain Vibration: Ignoring a failing Dual Mass Flywheel can eventually damage the transmission input shaft."
